IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`

-- Regulation 2 (interpretation), the definitions of two benefits that are made of several kinds of payment:
-- attendance allowance and war disablement pension. The other benefits in regulation 2 are one clause each and point to an Act
-- that is not among the inputs; they are constructors of `Benefit` in uc-core.l4.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- attendance allowance: five kinds of payment are listed; limb (c) is blank in this text (line 21), so the limbs are (a), (b),
-- (d), (e) and (f). Whether a payment is one of these is a stated input.
-- src:18 | “attendance allowance” means—
-- src:19 | (a) an attendance allowance under section 64 of the Contributions and Benefits Act;
-- src:20 | (b) an increase of disablement pension under section 104 or 105 of that Act (increases where constant attendance needed and for exceptionally severe disablement);
-- src:22 | (d) a payment by virtue of article 14, 15, 16, 43 or 44 of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983 or any analogous payment;
-- src:23 | (e) any payment based on the need for attendance which is paid as an addition to a war disablement pension;
-- src:24 | (f) armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011;
@ref reg 2 "attendance allowance" (src:18-24)
DECLARE `Payment that may be an attendance allowance` HAS
    `attendance allowance under section 64 of the Contributions and Benefits Act`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `increase of disablement pension under section 104 or 105 of that Act`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment by virtue of article 14, 15, 16, 43 or 44 of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983 or any analogous payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment based on the need for attendance which is paid as an addition to a war disablement pension`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:18 | “attendance allowance” means—
-- src:19 | (a) an attendance allowance under section 64 of the Contributions and Benefits Act;
-- src:20 | (b) an increase of disablement pension under section 104 or 105 of that Act (increases where constant attendance needed and for exceptionally severe disablement);
-- src:22 | (d) a payment by virtue of article 14, 15, 16, 43 or 44 of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983 or any analogous payment;
-- src:23 | (e) any payment based on the need for attendance which is paid as an addition to a war disablement pension;
-- src:24 | (f) armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011;
@ref reg 2 "attendance allowance" (src:18-24)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment that may be an attendance allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — attendance allowance` payment MEANS
    (payment's `attendance allowance under section 64 of the Contributions and Benefits Act`)
    OR (payment's `increase of disablement pension under section 104 or 105 of that Act`)
    OR (payment's `payment by virtue of article 14, 15, 16, 43 or 44 of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983 or any analogous payment`)
    OR (payment's `payment based on the need for attendance which is paid as an addition to a war disablement pension`)
    OR (payment's `armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- war disablement pension: any retired pay, pension or allowance payable in respect of disablement under an instrument specified
-- in section 639(2) of ITEPA. The list in that section is not among the inputs, so the last fact is a stated input.
-- src:112 | “war disablement pension” means any retired pay, pension or allowance payable in respect of disablement under an instrument specified in section 639(2) of ITEPA;
@ref reg 2 "war disablement pension" (src:112)
DECLARE `Payment that may be a war disablement pension` HAS
    `retired pay, pension or allowance`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable in respect of disablement`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable under an instrument specified in section 639(2) of ITEPA`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:112 | “war disablement pension” means any retired pay, pension or allowance payable in respect of disablement under an instrument specified in section 639(2) of ITEPA;
@ref reg 2 "war disablement pension" (src:112)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment that may be a war disablement pension`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — war disablement pension` payment MEANS
    (payment's `retired pay, pension or allowance`)
    AND (payment's `payable in respect of disablement`)
    AND (payment's `payable under an instrument specified in section 639(2) of ITEPA`)
